remuda: cluster join: quote the whole join line (it contains spaces); FINGERPRINT is optional on a terminal: remuda cluster join [FINGERPRINT] 'remuda-join-v1 …'
Join using a quoted invitation line; a fingerprint is needed when stdin is not a terminal. Example: remuda cluster join 'remuda-join-v1 …'

Usage: remuda cluster join [FINGERPRINT] 'JOIN_LINE' [--bind IP[:PORT]]

Arguments:
  [FINGERPRINT]  Optional fingerprint for non-terminal use
  [JOIN_LINE]    Quoted join line

Options:
  -h, --help              Print help
      --bind <IP[:PORT]>  Address; omitted port defaults to 7441

Next: remuda cluster join [FINGERPRINT] 'JOIN_LINE' [--bind IP[:PORT]]
